# The upper bound of a ball with a one-limb center, as a number of T (milestone2.md, "One
# enclosure interface", the row of lower_as and upper_as, and "The empty set and the whole line"):
# for a finite ball RU(c + r), the smallest number of T not below every member, in the
# format with overflow; the whole line gives +inf (0 + inf rounded up), and the empty ball
# -inf, by the select on the radius, which is a NaN exactly for the empty ball.
kernel:        ball_upper_as_1
input:         stored c
input:         stored r
output:        h
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       set_bound h above x x=c,r tight=rounded
min_precision: 2
source:        the center plus the radius, rounded up (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   h is selected after the test of the radius that tells the empty ball; set_bound states what comes out for each state of the ball

t  = add_up_1(c, r)
ne = eq(r, r)
mi = neg(const inf)
h  = select(ne, t, mi)
